  "name": "Hospital Clinical Network (IoMT)",
  "category": "mixed",
  "description": "Acute-care hospital: corporate LAN, clinical data-centre servers (EHR, HL7 interface engine, dcm4chee PACS, RIS, LIS, infusion-pump server), a vendor remote-service DMZ and medical-device VLANs. IMAGING: GE Revolution EVO CT and Siemens MAGNETOM Vida MRI push studies to the PACS over DICOM (C-ECHO + C-STORE; AE titles, implementation UIDs and the modality's manufacturer / model / serial / software in every data set), plus a Carestream DirectView CR 975 on Windows XP Embedded. PATIENT-MON: 12 Mindray BeneVision N17 monitors stream HL7 ORU^R01 vitals to the central station CMS01, which forwards them to the interface engine; the EHR feeds ADT^A01 to the engine, which fans out to RIS, LIS and the Rauland Responder 5 nurse-call server. INFUSION: 20 BD Alaris 8015 pumps check in with the pump server over TLS. BMS: Tridium JACE + JCI Metasys FECs on BACnet/IP (polls, Who-Is/I-Am, COV). Planted findings: (1) cleartext PHI — every HL7 v2 (MLLP, TCP 2575) and DICOM association carries patient demographics unencrypted; (2) EOL modality CR-LEGACY (Windows XP Embedded, SMBv1 to FILE01, MS08-067 / MS17-010 / BlueKeep); (3) infusion pump PUMP-017 talks directly to an internet host (external PUMP-VENDOR-CLOUD, 52.86.144.203) bypassing the proxy, while the MRI's sanctioned remote service goes through VENDOR-GW in the DMZ (external SIEMENS-SRS). Periods: DICOM pushes every 20-120 s, monitor ORU every 10 s, pump check-ins 60 s, BACnet polls 5 s.",
